    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for 2026-05-07 is anchored by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, whose 74.56 score marks him as our premier start. Facing Simeon Woods Richardson, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable SP_xERA of 4.85 and a strong +14% dynamic platoon edge, positioning him to capitalize on the weak opposing arm. **Gunnar Henderson** follows closely with a 69.76 rating; despite facing the formidable Max Meyer, **Gunnar Henderson** remains a must-start due to his leadoff role (+10%) and ability to mitigate Meyer\u2019s skill set. **Brady House** and **Nasim Nunez** are also slated for high-value outings against Woods Richardson, with **Brady House** showing particular promise at a 63.81 efficiency score, bolstered by a +9% platoon advantage that suggests a high probability for XBH production.\n\nThe decision to bench **Josh Jung** (55.82) was the most difficult call of the morning. While **Josh Jung** sits within the \"Marginal\" range, he was edged out by the superior platoon and order-slot projection for **Marcell Ozuna** and the overall matchup efficiency of our infield starters. While **Josh Jung**\u2019s matchup against Paul Blackburn is serviceable, the optimizer prioritized the higher cumulative point totals afforded to **Marcell Ozuna**, who manages a 59.48 despite a tougher draw against Zac Gallen. We remain cognizant that several positions remain subject to \"Lineup Pending\" volatility; should the confirmed lineups shift **Liam Hicks** or others out of favorable spots, we risk a downward adjustment on those efficiency scores. We are effectively punting on elite stolen base volume today to prioritize categorical efficiency, though we remain cautious of the volatility surrounding **Jackson Merrill**, whose 59.87 score is dampened by a -13% platoon penalty against the southpaw Matthew Liberatore.",
